    {
      "content": "#include <cstdio>\n#include <vector>\n#include <algorithm>\n\nstatic inline int read_int() {\n    int x = 0, sgn = 1;\n    char c = getchar_unlocked();\n    while (c <= ' ') c = getchar_unlocked();\n    if (c == '-') { sgn = -1; c = getchar_unlocked(); }\n    while (c >= '0' && c <= '9') {\n        x = x * 10 + (c - '0');\n        c = getchar_unlocked();\n    }\n    return sgn * x;\n}\n\nint main() {\n    int n = read_int();\n    int s = read_int();\n\n    std::vector<long long> II((n+1)*(n+1), 0);\n\n    for (int i = 0; i < n; ++i) {\n        long long hsum = 0;\n        int base_curr = (i+1)*(n+1);\n        int base_prev = i*(n+1);\n        #pragma GCC ivdep\n        for (int j = 0; j < n; ++j) {\n            int v = read_int();\n            hsum += v;\n            II[base_curr + j + 1] = II[base_prev + j + 1] + hsum;\n        }\n    }\n\n    const int BI = 32;\n    const int BJ = 64;\n    int mxSum = -2147483648;\n\n    for (int i0 = 0; i0 <= n - s; i0 += BI) {\n        int i_end = std::min(i0 + BI, n - s + 1);\n        for (int j0 = 0; j0 <= n - s; j0 += BJ) {\n            int j_end = std::min(j0 + BJ, n - s + 1);\n            for (int i = i0; i < i_end; ++i) {\n                long long *row_i   = &II[i*(n+1)];\n                long long *row_is  = &II[(i+s)*(n+1)];\n                #pragma GCC ivdep\n                for (int j = j0; j < j_end; ++j) {\n                    long long sub_sum = row_is[j+s] - row_i[j+s] - row_is[j] + row_i[j];\n                    if (sub_sum > mxSum)\n                        mxSum = static_cast<int>(sub_sum);\n                }\n            }\n        }\n    }\n\n    printf(\"%d\\n\", mxSum);\n    return 0;\n}\n",
      "path": "src/solution.cpp"
    }
  ],
  "hypothesis": "Tile the search loops over both i and j dimensions (block sizes BI=32, BJ=64) to improve temporal reuse of integral image rows across neighboring columns. Within each tile, iterate innermost over contiguous column indices for better spatial locality. Precompute row base pointers for the four corners outside the inner loop to avoid repeated index multiplication.",
